<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Android 11 and below. The Android 12+ equivalent is data_extraction_rules.xml,
    and the two have to agree.

    The saved controller address still travels, which is the part worth keeping:
    a new phone comes back pointed at the same wall.

    The database does not. Its schema is not migration-managed yet, so a file
    written by one build can be one this build refuses to open - which is
    exactly what happened to 0.11.0, where a restore put an in-development
    schema onto a fresh install and route saving was silently dead.

    ClimbDatabase now moves such a file aside rather than dying on it, but that
    turns a bad restore into routes that quietly disappear, which is no better
    from the outside. Until there are real migrations, routes move between
    devices deliberately - export to a file, import on the other side - and not
    by a mechanism that can only half work.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="database" path="climb.db" />
    <exclude domain="database" path="climb.db-wal" />
    <exclude domain="database" path="climb.db-shm" />
</full-backup-content>
